Subject: [PATCH] core: unwind partially initialized connection state

Base: PipeWire 1.6.11, 4287f31510771fc999f8a58a024c81ca10b8d55f
Apply after 0001-owned-remote-fd-on-setup-error.patch.

core_new creates a memory pool and object map before resolving the protocol.
A missing protocol, failed native client or failed proxy leaves those objects
allocated. A proxy failure also leaves its protocol client on the protocol's
client list, referring to the freed core. Check memory-pool creation and unwind
only the resources already initialized at each failure label.

The embedded core proxy has no core/proxy listeners until all fallible creation
has succeeded. pw_proxy_init removes its failed map entry; pw_proxy_new frees
its failed client proxy. Therefore this partial-construction path clears the
map directly instead of calling the connected-core teardown on a half object.

Reviewed core.c, proxy.c, mem.c, map.h and module-protocol-native.c at the fixed
revision. The core_new implementation is unchanged in upstream 685cb07a92acac24677fded669308f036207bb9a;
no matching upstream fix was found. Upstream MIT notices continue to apply.
This is a huhucapture adaptation, not an assertion of upstream acceptance.

diff --git a/src/pipewire/core.c b/src/pipewire/core.c
--- a/src/pipewire/core.c
+++ b/src/pipewire/core.c
@@ -339,6 +339,8 @@
 	p->context = context;
 	p->properties = properties;
 	p->pool = pw_mempool_new(NULL);
+	if (p->pool == NULL)
+		goto error_pool;
 	if (user_data_size > 0)
 		p->user_data = SPA_PTROFF(p, sizeof(struct pw_core), void);
 	p->proxy.user_data = p->user_data;
@@ -385,17 +387,24 @@
 	res = -errno;
 	pw_log_error("%p: can't create properties: %m", p);
 	goto exit_free;
+error_pool:
+	res = -errno;
+	pw_log_error("%p: can't create memory pool: %m", p);
+	goto exit_free;
 error_protocol:
 	pw_log_error("%p: can't find protocol '%s': %s", p, protocol_name, spa_strerror(res));
-	goto exit_free;
+	goto exit_pool;
 error_connection:
 	res = -errno;
 	pw_log_error("%p: can't create new native protocol connection: %m", p);
-	goto exit_free;
+	goto exit_pool;
 error_proxy:
 	pw_log_error("%p: can't initialize proxy: %s", p, spa_strerror(res));
-	goto exit_free;
-
+	pw_protocol_client_destroy(p->conn);
+
+exit_pool:
+	pw_map_clear(&p->objects);
+	pw_mempool_destroy(p->pool);
 exit_free:
 	free(p);
 exit_cleanup:
